Notebook[{
Cell["Forbidden suffixes and unbounded tail families for Rule 30", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["Troy Lowry; OpenAI Codex \[Bullet] 2026-10-23", "Author",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["\<\
For every finite Boolean word v, no column of a configuration with a leftmost \
black cell eventually repeats 0^r v 011 when r is at least 10|v|+41. Suffixes \
001001 and 111001 give the bound 10|v|+71. Unlike a list of bounded-length \
tails, these are families with unrestricted tail length. The complete \
standalone catalog proof and its dependencies pass the unchanged local \
official kernel checker at the pinned reference commit. This is a partial \
result. The notebook evaluates the included proof with LeanLink; prize-system \
submission and verification are separate steps.\
\>", "Abstract",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["Exact advance over the earlier essay", "Section",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let v be ",
 StyleBox["any",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Boolean word, including the empty word. Its length, number of black cells, \
and number of alternations are unrestricted. The following repeating words \
are impossible in any column of any configuration with a leftmost black \
cell:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"], Cell[
    "Repeating word", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
     Cell["Sufficient bound", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
     Cell["Strip width", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"0", "^", "r"}], " ", "v", " ", "011"}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{"r", " ", ">=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"10", "*", "length", 
        RowBox[{"(", "v", ")"}]}], "+", "41"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"], Cell[
    "5", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"0", "^", "r"}], " ", "v", " ", "001001"}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{"r", " ", ">=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"10", "*", "length", 
        RowBox[{"(", "v", ")"}]}], "+", "71"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"], Cell[
    "6", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"0", "^", "r"}], " ", "v", " ", "111001"}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{"r", " ", ">=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"10", "*", "length", 
        RowBox[{"(", "v", ")"}]}], "+", "71"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"], Cell[
    "6", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell["\<\
Consequently these exclusions hold for every column of every nonzero finite \
starting pattern and for the single-seed center, with no bound on the \
transient.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For example, choosing v=(10)^k excludes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"0", "^", "r"}], " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", "10", ")"}], "^", "k"}], " ", "011"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 " for every k>=0 and r>=20k+41. This includes tails longer than five bits. \
It does ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " exclude the alternating word itself: its long white run and terminal ",
 Cell[BoxData["011"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 " remain hypotheses."
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],

Cell["\<\
These results follow from the earlier analytic white-pulse theorem, together \
with small new full-set certificates. They do not replace the sharper \
short-tail bounds; many small instances overlap known families. Global \
novelty is not established.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell["Why an arbitrary prefix is allowed", "Section",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell["\<\
A width-K strip consists of the K cells immediately right of the proposed \
periodic column. Its left input is the column's driver bit. Both possible \
right inputs are allowed at every step, so the finite transition relation \
covers every actual evolution.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start from ",
 StyleBox["all",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " strip states, rather than a set reached after a particular zero run. A \
direct finite calculation proves that the suffix ",
 Cell[BoxData["011"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 " cannot produce the all-white width-five strip, regardless of the starting \
strip and right inputs. The same statement holds at width six for ",
 Cell[BoxData["001001"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["111001"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell["\<\
Whatever the prefix v does, the actual strip at the start of the suffix is \
one of those starting states. Therefore the strip contains a black cell at \
the next period start. This reasoning needs no bound or enumeration on v.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The earlier arbitrary-tail reduction says that a hypothetical periodic word \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"0", "^", "r"}], " ", "u"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 ", with r>=10|u|+11, keeps its right neighbor white at every phase s \
satisfying s+9(|u|+1)<=r. A black cell in a width-K strip at the period start \
reaches that neighbor in fewer than K white steps. If K+9(|u|+1)<=r, this \
contradicts the required white neighbor."
}], "Text",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],

Cell["\<\
Thus any suffix w with a vacuum-free full-set image supplies the general \
criterion\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell["    r >= max(10(|v|+|w|)+11, K+9(|v|+|w|+1)).", "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell["\<\
Substituting the three small certificates gives the bounds in the table. This \
is a deduction from a kernel-proved analytic theorem and exact finite facts, \
not an extrapolation from finitely many prefix lengths or padding lengths.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],

Cell["Executed independent computations", "Section",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],

Cell["\<\
A separate cellwise Python implementation enumerated every initial strip and \
every right-boundary history. It uses the Boolean Rule 30 rule directly, \
without Lean's packed bit update:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

