Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30WhitePulseResearch\\n\\n/- Source: \
lean/Ruliology/CellularAutomata/Rule30WhitePaddingVacuumCriterionResearch.\
lean -/\\n/-!\\n# A finite vacuum-avoidance criterion for arbitrary \
white-padding families\\n\\nA stable zero-driven reachable set G and the \
single finite check that a pulse u\\ncannot send G to the vacuum imply \
exclusions of 0^r u for all sufficiently large r.\\nThe length and contents \
of u are unrestricted. This does not establish that such\\nvacuum-avoidance \
certificates exist for every pulse.\\n-/\\nnamespace \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30WhitePaddingVacuumCriterionResearch\\nopen \
Rule30Jen Rule30Realization Rule30FiniteConfigs \
Rule30StripCertificates\\nopen Rule30WhitePaddingResearch \
Rule30WhitePulseResearch\\n\\n/-- A nonzero encoded strip contains a black \
cell within its width. -/\\ntheorem enc_nonzero_has_black {x : Int \
\[RightArrow] Bool} {K t : Nat} {i : Int} {v : Nat}\\n    (he : \
Rule30FiniteStripsResearch.Enc x K t i v) (hv : v \[NotEqual] 0) :\\n    \
\[Exists] j, j < K \[And] evol x t (i + (j + 1 : Nat)) = true := by\\n  \
obtain \:27e8j, hj\:27e9 := Nat.exists_testBit_of_ne_zero hv\\n  have hjK : j \
< K := by\\n    by_cases h : j < K\\n    \[CenterDot] exact h\\n    \
\[CenterDot] have hh := Nat.testBit_lt_two_pow\\n        (Nat.lt_of_lt_of_le \
he.1 (Nat.pow_le_pow_right (by decide) (show K \[LessEqual] j by omega)))\\n  \
